Subject: ps2xRuntime: VIF UNPACK takes STCYCL CL 0 as is (filling write without data)

UNPACK forced CL 0 to 1 (and WL 0 to 1). With CL < WL that is a filling write, and the game's masked
UNPACKs after STCYCL CL 0 WL 2 carry no data at all: every value comes from ROW/COL. Forcing CL to 1 made the
interpreter read one vector (16 bytes) of the following VIFcodes as data, slip, and skip opcodes until it
resynchronised, losing UNPACKs and MSCALs on the way. Rule of Rose's A164 event uses 1,790 of these per frame:
nearly every VU1 primitive came out with Z -48 and off-screen coordinates.

Now as PCSX2 (vifUnpackSetup): WL 0 means 256, CL is used as is, a filling write reads CL * (NUM / WL) +
min(NUM % WL, CL) vectors, and a VIF1 UNPACK without data still writes its NUM vectors from the mask.

